        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0336" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg276"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 502.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch, No. 350, of the
                    8th instant, relative to the case of Mr. Waller, I have to inform you that on
                    the 9th instant a telegram was received by the Department from the United States
                    consul at Port Louis, Mauritius, stating that Mr. Waller’s family were to sail
                    for France on the 20th instant.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
